## You

Copy dari sini:
Build a web app called sainbyte using React + Vite + Tailwind + Firebase (Firestore + Auth).

No GAS, no Google Sheets. All data from Firestore. Start with EMPTY database, no dummy data, no placeholder, no demo content. Empty state must show "Belum ada data" with a button to add new.

Tech & Deploy:
- Frontend will be pushed to GitHub and deployed to Vercel. Use environment variables for Firebase config.
- Use Firebase Firestore for database, Firebase Auth for login.
- Use React Router with 2 routes: / and /developer.

Route 1: / - Public Decoy Page
This is the home page that looks like a simple project list. Keep it clean and innocent.
- Header text: sainbyte, subheader: dashboard list project. No logo icon, no favicon, no icon box.
- List of project links in card layout. Each card: title, description, URL, category, click count, last updated.
- Features: search, filter by category, category totals, add/edit/delete link (admin only, with password/PIN prompt), drag-drop reorder, export/import JSON, copy link button.
- Global chatbox at bottom: visitors can comment with free optional name, animated emotes, reply to comment with quote, like comment, admin can pin 1 comment and delete comment. Show optimistic sending animation, do not wait for server to show bubble.
- Visit counter at footer with count-up animation.
- Design rules: mobile content width is 80% centered, no horizontal scroll, pinch zoom must work. All popups/modals must be centered, not bottom sheet. Support mobile site and desktop site mode.
- Themes: dark/light + other accent colors (green, blue, purple, orange). Auto follow system theme, manual choice wins. Fix light theme: no black text on black background.
- PWA installable.

Hidden Trigger:
- Tapping the sainbyte header logo 5 times quickly navigates to /developer. No visible button to developer page.

Route 2: /developer - Real Private Dashboard
This is the real dashboard, UI must look TOTALLY different from /. Dense, admin panel style, sidebar layout on desktop, bottom nav on mobile. Dark theme by default.
- Must NOT be indexed by search engines. Add noindex.
- If not logged in, show only login page. Login with Google and Email. No data is visible before login.
- After login, show: Overview stats (total projects, total visits, total clicks, total comments), Projects table (full CRUD with search, sort, filter), Comments moderation table, Visits & Clicks analytics (simple chart/table per day).
- Add a generic Database section: user can create custom collections (like Notes, Finance, Todo) from scratch, each collection has its own table with add/edit/delete, search, filter. This is for future personal data.
- All developer data is private. Firestore rules: public can only read public projects/comments on /. Developer collections can only be read/written by logged-in owner.

Firestore Collections (start empty):
- projects: title, description, url, category, clicks, createdAt, updatedAt
- comments: name, message, replyToId, replyToName, replyToMessage, likes, pinned, createdAt
- visits: total, today, lastVisit
- customCollections: for generic database in developer page

General Rules:
- All UI text in Bahasa Indonesia.
- No placeholder data, no lorem ipsum.
- Smooth animations, no laggy transitions.
- Mobile first, must work perfectly on Android browser.

